    (v_topic_id, 'A 61-old male with mucous membrane pemphigoid is found to have high titers of autoantibodies targeting Laminin-332 (epiligrin). What is the critical clinical implication of this specific subtype of pemphigoid?', '["Spontaneous resolution without scarring", "Excellent response to Dapsone without systemic steroids", "Association with HLA-DQ2 and Celiac Disease", "Rapid progression to acute respiratory distress syndrome", "Significantly increased risk of an underlying solid malignancy (e.g., adenocarcinomas)"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Anti-Laminin-332 (epiligrin) mucous membrane pemphigoid is strongly associated with an increased risk of an underlying solid organ malignancy, particularly adenocarcinomas of the gastrointestinal or genitourinary tracts. Patients diagnosed with this subtype require age-appropriate cancer screenings.'),
